# Software update: the standing choices, and every outcome of a check the
# simulator can stage. Each choice is read back where the owner looks for
# it: the row that opens the choices and the Software update row at home.
# The home list can reflow between pages at the largest text size when a
# summary gets shorter, so the route finds the home row by what it says.
wait-for Settings
tap-paged Software update
wait-for Check for updates
expect Stable · Cobalt and apps update on their own
tap Channel and automatic updates
wait-for Update Cobalt automatically
# Each switch applies on the tap. At the largest sizes the lines under the
# switches give way, so the rows outside this screen are what is read.
tap-id auto-cobalt
wait-idle
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Stable · Apps update on their own
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Settings
maybe-tap-id previous
tap-paged Stable · Apps update on their own
wait-for Check for updates
tap Channel and automatic updates
wait-for Update apps automatically
tap-id auto-apps
wait-idle
shot settings-update-switches-off
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Stable · Updates only when you ask
# Going to the background and back keeps them.
lifecycle background
lifecycle foreground
wait-idle
expect Stable · Updates only when you ask
# The simulator keeps these choices in memory for one session, so a restart
# here would prove nothing; the reader keeps them on its storage.
tap Channel and automatic updates
wait-for Update Cobalt automatically
# Choosing the channel already chosen asks nothing.
tap-id channel-stable
wait-idle
expect Update options
expect-missing Confirm update channel
# The other channel asks first, says what changes and what is kept, and
# both Back and Cancel leave the channel alone.
tap-id channel-beta
wait-for Confirm update channel
expect Current channel
expect New channel
expect your saved keys are kept
expect Use Beta updates
expect Cancel
shot settings-update-confirm-beta
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Update Cobalt automatically
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Stable · Updates only when you ask
tap Channel and automatic updates
tap-id channel-beta
wait-for Use Beta updates
tap Use Beta updates
wait-for Update Cobalt automatically
expect-missing Confirm update channel
shot settings-update-options-beta
# Changing the channel keeps the switches as they were.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Beta · Updates only when you ask
expect Check for updates
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Settings
maybe-tap-id previous
tap-paged Beta · Updates only when you ask
wait-for Check for updates
tap Channel and automatic updates
tap-id channel-stable
wait-for Use Stable updates
expect Nothing is downgraded
shot settings-update-confirm-stable
tap Use Stable updates
wait-for Update Cobalt automatically
tap-id auto-cobalt
wait-idle
tap-id auto-apps
wait-idle
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Stable · Cobalt and apps update on their own
# A server that does not answer is a different sentence from no Wi-Fi, and
# Try again on its banner checks again.
scenario host-down
tap Check for updates
wait-for The update server did not answer.
expect Try again
expect-missing Check for updates
expect Channel and automatic updates
shot settings-update-host-down
scenario network-timeout
tap Try again
wait-for The update server did not answer.
# A runtime that refuses Settings the network is not blamed on Wi-Fi.
scenario permission-denied
tap Try again
wait-for Settings is not allowed to use the network
expect-missing not on Wi-Fi
shot settings-update-not-allowed
# No Wi-Fi offers the way to join one, and the home row says the same.
scenario offline
tap Try again
wait-for This reader is not on Wi-Fi.
expect Join Wi-Fi
expect Check again
expect-missing Try again
# Back from the Wi-Fi page it opens returns here, to check again.
tap Join Wi-Fi
wait-for-id toggle
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for This reader is not on Wi-Fi.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Settings
maybe-tap-id previous
tap-paged Not on Wi-Fi
wait-for This reader is not on Wi-Fi.
shot settings-update-offline-again
tap Check again
wait-for This reader is not on Wi-Fi.
# Changing the channel starts over: the old channel's answer is cleared.
scenario normal
tap Channel and automatic updates
tap-id channel-beta
tap Use Beta updates
wait-for Update Cobalt automatically
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Check for updates
expect-missing This reader is not on Wi-Fi.
expect Beta · Cobalt and apps update on their own
# A choice the runtime will not keep is said over the choices, and the
# switch stays as it was. Once a later choice is kept, nothing on the
# update screen should still report the refusal.
scenario permission-denied
tap Channel and automatic updates
tap-id auto-apps
wait-for Cobalt did not allow Settings to do that.
shot settings-update-choice-refused
scenario normal
tap-id auto-apps
wait-idle
expect-missing Cobalt did not allow Settings to do that.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Beta · Cobalt updates on its own
shot settings-update-after-refusal
expect-missing Cobalt did not allow Settings to do that.
expect Check for updates
